* A string laid out in cells, printed by a scan loop -- the shape that makes
* the expander lose track of the cursor, and @here the way back.
*
* The letters are written as letters. `+{'H'}` and `+{72}` expand to the same
* seventy-two plus signs; only one of them says what it is for.

@var first
@var second
@var third
@var after at 3

@to first
+{'H'}
@to second
+{'i'}
@to third
+{'!'}

@to first
[
    .
    >
]

* The scan stopped on the terminator, which is `after`. The expander cannot
* know that; saying so costs nothing and emits nothing.
@here after
@to after
+{'\n'}
.
